When generating a Git commit message, use Conventional Commits.

Format:
<type>: <description>

Types: feat, fix, style, refactor, docs, chore, perf, test, ci, build

Rules:
- One short subject line, imperative mood, under 72 characters
- No period at the end of the subject
- Do not write a prose paragraph summarizing every file
- Add a body only if the change is non-obvious
- Prefer feat for new UI/content, style for CSS-only tweaks, refactor for no-behavior changes, fix for bug fixes
